{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463684",
      "title": "Different Ways of Using Vue",
      "lectureOrder": 3,
      "videoOrder": 3,
      "sourceHash": "c7beef8a7e7bff53bb8223128b9612bf1ca840ad3a606b09da51d64a80603de5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 5.45,
          "en": "So, now you have a rough idea of what Vue is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.45,
          "end": 7.88,
          "en": "and why you might want to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.88,
          "end": 10.92,
          "en": "In case you're not fully convinced yet, no worries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.92,
          "end": 14.17,
          "en": "We'll see it all in action very soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.17,
          "end": 16.57,
          "en": "There is one important thing to realize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.57,
          "end": 19.23,
          "en": "about using Vue, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.23,
          "end": 24.23,
          "en": "We can use Vue in two main ways, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.32,
          "end": 28.98,
          "en": "We can use it to control parts of an HTML page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.98,
          "end": 32.9,
          "en": "and make that part a bit more reactive and interactive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.9,
          "end": 34.15,
          "en": "So, we could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.15,
          "end": 37.29,
          "en": "control the sidebar on a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.29,
          "end": 39.68,
          "en": "to load elements there dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.68,
          "end": 41.78,
          "en": "or we have a chat overlay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.78,
          "end": 43.28,
          "en": "which the user can open up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.28,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "and that chat overlay is controlled by Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 49.75,
          "en": "So, we don't have to control everything on the page with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.75,
          "end": 52.41,
          "en": "We don't have to use Vue for everything on a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.41,
          "end": 54.68,
          "en": "if we don't have any reactivity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.68,
          "end": 57.53,
          "en": "If we don't need an interactive element somewhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.53,
          "end": 60.52,
          "en": "on our screen, we don't have to use Vue for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.52,
          "end": 64.86,
          "en": "And we can therefore use Vue to build so-called Widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.86,
          "end": 66.93,
          "en": "And that's not a general term,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.93,
          "end": 69.19,
          "en": "that's just a term I came up with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.19,
          "end": 72.92,
          "en": "We control parts of a page by dumping in small Widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.92,
          "end": 75.76,
          "en": "like a chat screen, like a interactive sidebar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.76,
          "end": 78.11,
          "en": "and other parts on the page are totally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.11,
          "end": 80.453,
          "en": "not affected by Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.58,
          "end": 85,
          "en": "The opposite, the other way of using Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85,
          "end": 86.81,
          "en": "would be that everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.81,
          "end": 89.64,
          "en": "on a page is controlled with Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.64,
          "end": 93.81,
          "en": "So, every element is rendered and controlled by Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.81,
          "end": 97.31,
          "en": "This is the so-called Single-Page-Application approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.31,
          "end": 101.50999999999999,
          "en": "where the server only ever sends one HTML page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.50999999999999,
          "end": 104.55,
          "en": "which includes basically no markup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.55,
          "end": 107.71000000000001,
          "en": "but all the script imports we need importing Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.71000000000001,
          "end": 109.43,
          "en": "and our Vue code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.43,
          "end": 112.08,
          "en": "And thereafter, our Vue code defines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.08,
          "end": 114.31,
          "en": "what should be rendered on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.31,
          "end": 117.75,
          "en": "in the browser after the page was loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.75,
          "end": 119.68,
          "en": "Now, there also are some mixtures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.68,
          "end": 121.73,
          "en": "but you will learn all about that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.73,
          "end": 123.95,
          "en": "all about those two approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.95,
          "end": 126.32,
          "en": "in great detail throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.32,
          "end": 128.5,
          "en": "We're going to start with the left approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 128.5,
          "end": 131.1,
          "en": "because that's easier to get into Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.1,
          "end": 133.39,
          "en": "but we'll then also move to the other approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.39,
          "end": 136,
          "en": "to the everything is controlled by Vue approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136,
          "end": 137.56,
          "en": "so that by the end of the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.56,
          "end": 140.67000000000002,
          "en": "you feel comfortable using either of the two approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.67000000000002,
          "end": 144,
          "en": "and you will also know when to use which approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144,
          "end": 146.7,
          "en": "because it turns out, there is no better approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.7,
          "end": 150.16,
          "en": "These approaches are simply good for different things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.16,
          "end": 151.26,
          "en": "And throughout the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.26,
          "end": 153.623,
          "en": "this will become very, very clear.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
